suggestions.sketch:
Create four new classes—OrderRepository (handles _orders, _next_id, place/get/cancel/etc.), PricingEngine (holds _tax_rate, _discount_rules and methods set_discount, apply_tax, total_with_tax, shipping_for, bulk_discount), AuditLog (manages _log and related methods), and Notifier (stores _smtp_host, _sent and notification methods). The original OrderManager becomes a thin façade that composes these services:

class OrderManager:
    def __init__(self):
        self.repo = OrderRepository()
        self.pricing = PricingEngine()
        self.audit = AuditLog()
        self.notifier = Notifier()
    # delegate calls, e.g.
    def place_order(self, customer, lines):
        return self.repo.place_order(customer, lines)
    # similarly forward other methods.

Each new class encapsulates its own private attributes, reducing the method‑attribute graph to a single component per class, thus lowering LCOM4. The overall DCC rises because OrderManager now references four additional classes, but the trade‑off is improved modularity and testability.

